{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), we have essentially no information about whether the image modality carries useful signal. The most consequential fork in this search space is whether image features are informative at all, because it determines whether the ~36 multimodal configurations are worth exploring. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest test of this question: it matches the baseline on profile_setting (singleprofile) and isolates the modality/representation axis. If image_only performs comparably to or better than the RNA baseline, it justifies investing subsequent experiments in multimodal fusion. If it performs substantially worse, it signals that RNA is the dominant modality and we should focus on RNA encoder and profile-setting variations instead. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the largest design decision before committing budget to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

